  facts:
  - Preservatives stop bacteria from growing so food stays safe longer.
  - Salt is one of the oldest food preservatives, used for thousands of years.
  - Sugar preserves jams by pulling water away from microbes.
  - Preservatives help prevent food poisoning, not just spoilage.
  - Vitamin C is used as a preservative to stop fruits from turning brown.
  - Antioxidants keep oils and snacks from becoming rancid.
  - Sodium benzoate works best in acidic foods like soft drinks.
  - Preservatives help reduce food waste by extending shelf life.
  - Dried fruits last longer because of preservatives like sulfites.
  - Some preservatives occur naturally in foods like lemon and vinegar.
  - Preservatives protect both food quality and food safety.
  - Without preservatives, many packaged foods would spoil in days.
  - "Fiber slows down sugar absorption \u2014 so foods with fiber are usually healthier."
  - Antioxidants slow down the aging process of food.
  - Preservatives play a key role in modern food safety systems.
  - Refrigeration alone is not always enough to preserve processed foods.
  - Preservatives can target bacteria, yeast, mold, or oxidation.
